---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import PwaHead from "../components/PwaHead.astro";
import { computeGuideStats } from "../lib/guide-stats";
import { generateContourLayer } from "../lib/contours";
// Same self-hosted fonts + token base as the hub — one theme, every surface.
import "@fontsource-variable/literata/standard.css";
import "@fontsource-variable/literata/standard-italic.css";
import "@fontsource-variable/atkinson-hyperlegible-next";
import "../styles/base.css";
import "../styles/about.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");

// Real numbers, counted from the guides at build time — never hand-typed.
// Same source of truth as the hub's stats beat.
const guides = await getCollection("guides");
const stats = computeGuideStats(guides.map((g) => g.data));

// One quiet contour field behind the hero — the overture's cartography, reused.
const contours = [
  generateContourLayer({ seed: 11, rings: 8, cx: 300, cy: 260 }),
  generateContourLayer({ seed: 29, rings: 6, cx: 760, cy: 420 }),
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>About — Waypoint</title>
    <meta name="description" content="How Waypoint builds verified, personalized travel guides: two independent research passes, automated verification gates, a fresh-eyes critic, and honest marks on anything unconfirmed." />
    <PwaHead />
    <!-- Dark-mode init — runs before paint to avoid flash (same as the hub). -->
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        const s = localStorage.getItem("tg-theme");
        const preferDark = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme:dark)").matches;
        if (s === "dark" || (s === null && preferDark)) {
          document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", "dark");
        } else if (s === "light") {
          document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", "light");
        }
      })();
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#aboutMain">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="ab-bar">
      <a class="ab-wordmark" href={`${base}/`}>← Waypoint</a>
    </header>

    <main class="about" id="aboutMain">
      <div class="ab-contours" aria-hidden="true">
        {contours.map((layer, i) => (
          <svg data-ab-contour={i} viewBox={`0 0 ${layer.viewBox} ${layer.viewBox}`} preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice">
            {layer.rings.map((points) => <polyline points={points} />)}
          </svg>
        ))}
      </div>

      <header class="ab-hero">
        <p class="ab-eyebrow">About Waypoint</p>
        <h1>Travel guides that show their work.</h1>
        <p class="ab-dek">
          Waypoint builds one-of-a-kind trip guides around real travelers, then proves every
          fact. Every price, hour, and door is checked against a <b>primary source</b> and
          stamped with the date we checked it. Nothing here is autogenerated and left unread.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="ab-stats" aria-label="Counted from the guides themselves">
        <div><div class="ab-stat-n">{stats.guideCount}</div><div class="ab-stat-l">Trips, fully planned</div></div>
        <div><div class="ab-stat-n">{stats.verifiedFactCount}</div><div class="ab-stat-l">Facts traced to a source</div></div>
        <div><div class="ab-stat-n">{stats.sourceCount}</div><div class="ab-stat-l">Distinct primary sources</div></div>
        <p class="ab-stats-note">Counted from the guides at build time, never typed in — the same honesty rule the guides live by.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="ab-sec" aria-labelledby="abValuesHead">
        <h2 class="ab-sec-head" id="abValuesHead">The four promises</h2>
        <p class="ab-sec-sub">A guide isn't finished until it keeps all four. Miss one and it doesn't ship.</p>
        <div class="ab-values">
          <article class="ab-value">
            <div class="ab-value-mark" aria-hidden="true">Verified</div>
            <p>Every perishable fact — a price, an opening hour, a timetable — traces to a primary
            source, with the date it was checked. When a fact ages past its shelf life, a weekly
            recheck re-verifies it against that same source.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="ab-value">
            <div class="ab-value-mark" aria-hidden="true">Personal</div>
            <p>A guide starts from one party's ranked priorities and the event the trip is built
            around. Depth goes where you actually care; the generic filler a search engine would
            give you gets cut.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="ab-value">
            <div class="ab-value-mark" aria-hidden="true">Actionable</div>
            <p>Every venue answers four questions before it earns a place: where is it, how do you
            get there, when does it fit your day, and do you need to book.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="ab-value">
            <div class="ab-value-mark" aria-hidden="true">Honest</div>
            <p>What we couldn't confirm is marked ⚠ or left out — never invented. An admitted
            blank beats a confident guess, every time.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ab-sec" aria-labelledby="abMarksHead">
        <h2 class="ab-sec-head" id="abMarksHead">Read the marks</h2>
        <p class="ab-sec-sub">Guides wear their evidence in the open. Three marks tell you exactly how much to trust a line.</p>
        <div class="ab-legend">
          <div class="ab-legend-row">
            <span class="ab-legend-chip">≈ €12</span>
            <p>Checked against a source, stated approximately — expect small drift, not surprises.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ab-legend-row">
            <span class="ab-legend-chip is-warn">⚠ unconfirmed</span>
            <p>We looked and couldn't confirm it. The gap is admitted, not papered over — re-check this one before you go.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ab-legend-row">
            <span class="ab-legend-chip is-ok">Checked 2026-07-23</span>
            <p>The date a fact was last verified. Each guide signs its own verified-fact count in its footer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ab-sec" aria-labelledby="abRouteHead">
        <h2 class="ab-sec-head" id="abRouteHead">How a guide is made</h2>
        <p class="ab-sec-sub">Every guide rides the same route — six stations, most of them automated, none of them skippable.</p>
        <ol class="ab-route">
          <li class="ab-stop">
            <p class="ab-stop-kicker">Station 1</p>
            <h3>Intake — your trip, ranked</h3>
            <p>Dates, party, budget, pace, and the <b>anchor event</b> the trip is built around,
            with your priorities ranked 1-2-3. This short form becomes the spec every later
            station obeys — and the bar the finished guide is judged against.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="ab-stop">
            <p class="ab-stop-kicker">Station 2</p>
            <h3>Research — twice, independently</h3>
            <p>Two research passes that never see each other's work. One climbs official,
            primary sources for the backbone: entry rules, transit, hours, prices. The other
            comes at the destination from the <b>resident's side</b> — local forums, blogs,
            video transcripts — hunting off-peak windows, crowd reality, and the places locals
            actually go.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="ab-stop">
            <p class="ab-stop-kicker">Station 3</p>
            <h3>Reconcile — the two drafts argue it out</h3>
            <p>Where both passes agree, confidence is high. Where they conflict, the conflict is
            resolved to the truth and the winning source recorded. Where the obvious pick turns
            out to be a tourist trap, a verified local alternative takes its place — with the
            best time to go.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="ab-stop">
            <p class="ab-stop-kicker">Station 4</p>
            <h3>Verify — the gates</h3>
            <p>Automated checks refuse the guide until every fact carries a source and a date,
            every day of the itinerary lines up, every link is alive, and every photo is real.
            What can't be sourced after honest effort is flagged ⚠ — <b>never invented</b>.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="ab-stop">
            <p class="ab-stop-kicker">Station 5</p>
            <h3>The Critic — fresh eyes, one question</h3>
            <p>A reviewer that never saw the research reads the finished guide against your spec
            and asks of every recommendation: <b>“would a generic AI have suggested this?”</b>
            Anything that fails is replaced with something researched for you, or it doesn't
            pass.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="ab-stop is-live">
            <p class="ab-stop-kicker">Station 6</p>
            <h3>Live — and kept alive</h3>
            <p>The guide publishes with live weather, holidays, and currency wired in. A weekly
            sweep re-verifies anything past its shelf life. And after the trip, what actually
            happened feeds back in — the guide gains a Plan&nbsp;⇄&nbsp;Actual view, and the
            next guide starts smarter about how you really travel.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="ab-cta" aria-labelledby="abCtaHead">
        <h2 class="ab-sec-head" id="abCtaHead" style="display:inline-block">See it in practice</h2>
        <p>The proof is in the guides — open one and look for the marks.</p>
        <a class="ab-cta-btn" href={`${base}/`}>Browse the guides →</a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="ab-foot">Waypoint — every fact checked, every route tested.</footer>
  </body>
</html>
